{"id": 32, "ts": 1780607516.6301293, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s thorough comparison of Candidate\u202fC\u2019s reliability and calmness with the concerns around Candidate\u202fD. However, the key trade\u2011off remains between C\u2019s excellent reliability and technical competence versus B\u2019s strong operational reliability and stress resilience, coupled with solid technical judgment on weather\u2014critical for long\u2011distance flights. While Sarah confirmed she has no direct observations of Candidate\u202fB\u2019s adaptability or feedback orientation, the lack of evidence does not yet indicate a deficiency; it simply highlights a gap we should probe later. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas and being perceived as egocentric could undermine crew cooperation and professional communication, which are essential in the cockpit. Given B\u2019s proven conscientiousness, effective stress handling, and technical skill set, I maintain my provisional recommendation for **Candidate\u202fB**, pending further insight on his adaptability."}
