{"id": 39, "ts": 1780607559.5124, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s stress resilience and weather\u2011assessment skill, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the stronger overall fit. James highlighted C\u2019s 100\u202f% reliability, calmness in crisis, rapid correct decision\u2011making, and ability to foster a positive crew atmosphere\u2014each directly addresses our core safety criteria. While we lack a concrete incident illustrating C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas, the same source also notes that he creates a positive atmosphere with his crew, suggesting that any communication shortfall has not yet undermined teamwork. In contrast, Emily reported B\u2019s uncooperative and grumpy demeanor, which are concrete behaviors that could erode crew cooperation, plus James mentioned B\u2019s weak memory for numbers, raising concerns about attention to detail. Given the decisive importance of reliability, calm decision\u2011making, and crew morale on long\u2011distance flights, I would provisionally recommend **Candidate\u202fC**."}
